{"parentUuid":null,"isSidechain":true,"promptId":"8b9c6287-d7e2-4fd6-8dbd-dc6c5dce5337","agentId":"a8815636d6b92c427","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"No subagents/forks, no commits/pushes. Token-efficient: read only what you edit; 5 checks; one 400px screenshot; report under 100 words. Your files: NEW cuore/web/electrical_routes.py, cuore/web/electrical_svg.py, cuore/web/templates/electrical.html, cuore/web/templates/_electrical_path.html, cuore/web/static/electrical.css, cuore/tests/check_electrical_page.py; small edits: _vbar.html (Electrical tab after Systems if present else after Timeline), code.html (include _electrical_path.html under the system badges), report.html (an \"Electrical path\" section per open code). Do not edit app.py (report include line), api/*, services/*, mes-log-mcp/*, systems_* files (another agent).\n\nRepo C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers; cuore FastAPI + Jinja, phone-first (44px targets; classes at the end of cuore/web/static/cuore.css; status colours; dark/light variables); server-rendered SVG only (pattern cuore/web/timeline_svg.py). Python .venv\\Scripts\\python.exe. A data agent is building in parallel cuore/services/electrical_bridge.py with elements() -> {id: {kind, label, location: {zone, description, source, confidence}, feeds, part_of_systems, tsb_refs, inspection_hint, notes}}, code_path(code) -> {code, path: [{id, role, kind, label, location, source, confidence}], systems_interaction: [{system, how, confidence, source}], inspect_steps: [{element, what, how, source}]}, inspections(vin) / latest(vin, element) -> {at, by, condition, note, media_ids}, add_inspection(vin, element, by, condition, note). Develop against a fixture until it lands; import lazily; degrade gracefully.\n\nBuild: (1) /v/{vin}/electrical page: a car LAYOUT diagram as SVG: a simple top-down car outline with zones (engine bay, dash, cabin driver/passenger, trunk, underbody, each wheel well) and the elements placed in their zone as labelled nodes (fuse box, grounds, connectors, modules, battery); node colour = latest inspection condition (green ok, amber loose/chafed/corroded/water, red not_found, grey never inspected); ?code=P0455 highlights that code's path (thick line through its elements in order, others dimmed); tap node -> element card. Element cards: kind, location in plain words with source+confidence, what it feeds, systems, inspection hint, latest condition, \"Record inspection\" form (condition buttons 44px, note, by; plain POST to /v/{vin}/electrical/inspect -> bridge add_inspection; redirect back), photo attach via the media strip if the `media_strip` Jinja global is defined (target_kind \"electrical\", target_id element id). Legend. (2) _electrical_path.html for code pages: the ordered path as a horizontal stepper (fuse -> connector -> component -> ground) with each hop's location, confidence chip, latest condition, and the \"how each system interacts with this problem\" list; \"Open in layout\" link to /v/{vin}/electrical?code=. (3) Tests: electrical page 200 with svg and legend; ?code=P0455 highlights (path class present); inspection POST round trip shows the condition; code page shows the path stepper; no horizontal overflow at 400px (CDP pattern from cuore/tests/check_live_widgets.py, cleanup via _edge_cleanup.py), one screenshot in the scratchpad. Run + check_api.py."},"uuid":"72778c79-0774-44af-ba28-5b42dcd55600","timestamp":"2026-10-08T02:44:02.096Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
