{"parentUuid":"dfa73982-562f-4c8b-8962-825a628ab8b2","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a8815636d6b92c427","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Cfp1qxjzQZnznyV6iNWtE","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_013ARNZX8WaK9ixs5pa13bDp","name":"SubagentHandback","input":{"message":"Built the electrical feature end-to-end, all 12 checks in check_electrical_page.py pass (including check_api.py as a companion run).\n\nNew files:\n- cuore/web/electrical_routes.py — GET /v/{vin}/electrical (?code= highlights that code's path), POST /v/{vin}/electrical/inspect. Lazily imports cuore.services.electrical_bridge (elements/code_path/inspections/latest/add_inspection per the given contract); falls back to a built-in fixture (EVAP path: fuse_f23 -> conn_c1_pcm -> purge_valve -> ground_g101 for P0440/P0455/P0456; a network path for U0100/U0101) when the bridge isn't wired yet. Registers `electrical_path_for(vin, code)` as a Jinja global on the shared cuore.web.routes templates env, same pattern as timeline_routes's `code_feel`. NOT registered in app.py (per instructions) — two lines documented in the module docstring for whoever wires it in.\n- cuore/web/electrical_svg.py — server-rendered inline SVG: top-down car outline with 10 zones (engine bay/dash/cabin driver+passenger/trunk/underbody + 4 wheel wells) plus an \"other\" zone for unplaced elements; nodes colored by latest inspection condition; `path_ids` draws a thick polyline + numbered rings through a code's path and dims everything else. Legend embedded in the SVG. Both the connector line and the path-highlight rings carry `class=\"path-hop\"`.\n- cuore/web/templates/electrical.html, _electrical_path.html, cuore/web/static/electrical.css — diagram page with element cards (location/feeds/systems/TSBs/inspection hint, 44px condition-button form via the existing `.tag-chip` pattern, media strip under target_kind \"electrical\"); the stepper partial (fuse→connector→component→ground, confidence + condition chips, systems-interaction list, \"Open in layout\" link).\n- cuore/tests/check_electrical_page.py — 12 checks: page 200 w/ svg+legend, ?code= highlight carries path-hop class, inspection POST round-trips and shows the condition, code page shows the stepper, check_api.py still exits 0, and a 400px CDP screenshot/overflow check (screenshot at cuore/tests → scratchpad/electrical_phone.png, no horizontal overflow).\n\nSmall edits (re-read each file first since a parallel \"systems\" agent had already landed changes):\n- cuore/web/templates/_vbar.html — added an Electrical tab; a Systems tab had already landed, so Electrical went right after it (per the fallback rule).\n- cuore/web/templates/code.html — added `{% include \"_electrical_path.html\" %}` right under the already-landed `_system_badge.html` include.\n- cuore/web/templates/report.html — added a new `<section id=\"electrical\">` right after the already-landed \"Systems involved\" section, looping view.open_work's codes and including `_electrical_path.html` per open code.\n\nDid not touch app.py, api/*, services/*, mes-log-mcp/*, or any systems_* files."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":477,"cache_read_input_tokens":229414,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":477,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_013ARNZX8WaK9ixs5pa13bDp":{"message":"Built the electrical feature end-to-end, all 12 checks in check_electrical_page.py pass (including check_api.py as a companion run).\n\nNew files:\n- cuore/web/electrical_routes.py — GET /v/{vin}/electrical (?code= highlights that code's path), POST /v/{vin}/electrical/inspect. Lazily imports cuore.services.electrical_bridge (elements/code_path/inspections/